<title>BELGIUM: ATHLETICS-FRANCE FAVOURITE FOR 1998 CROSS COUNTRY VENUE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-FRANCE FAVOURITE FOR 1998 CROSS COUNTRY VENUE.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLEROI, Belgium 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain, France, Italy, Slovenia and Spain have applied to stage the 1998 European cross country championships.</p>
<p>France are believed to be the favourites. The country has never staged the event and the French federation has suggested the northern coastal town of Le Touquet as the venue.</p>
<p>A decision will be taken at the European Athletic Association council meeting in Lisbon early next year.</p>
<p>Faro in Portugal will stage the 1997 championships.</p>
</text>
